error[E4017]: cannot use '+=' on an element of 'xs': the consuming 'Text.plus' would move it out, and only a whole variable can be moved and assigned back
  --> main.prism:12:5
   12 |     xs[i] += t
      |     ^
   = help: declare it with a shared receiver, 'operator fun Text.plus', which borrows the target in place
   = help: or move the value into a 'var', use '+=' on it there and put the result back
error[E4017]: cannot use '+=' on field 't' of 'h': the consuming 'Text.plus' would move it out, and only a whole variable can be moved and assigned back
  --> main.prism:16:5
   16 |     h.t += t
      |     ^
   = help: declare it with a shared receiver, 'operator fun Text.plus', which borrows the target in place
   = help: or move the value into a 'var', use '+=' on it there and put the result back
